.TH ANONCHAIN 1 "2026" "anonchain 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
anonchain \- multi-hop chain proxy interface + tool launcher
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B anonchain
.RI [ command " [" args ...]"]
.SH DESCRIPTION
ANONCHAIN is a chain proxy interface. Without arguments it opens a
terminal UI to test proxies, build a multi-hop chain and arm an
iptables kill-switch. With arguments it runs the given command
through the active chain.
.SH USAGE
.TP
.B anonchain
Open the TUI.
.TP
.B anonchain curl https://ifconfig.me
Run curl through the active chain (HTTP_PROXY + LD_PRELOAD).
.TP
.B anonchain nmap -sT -Pn scanme.nmap.org
Run nmap; TCP connect is tunneled via SOCKS5 LD_PRELOAD shim.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ANONCHAIN_PORT
Local chain proxy port (default 9050).
.TP
.B ANONCHAIN_PRELOAD
auto|on|off — control LD_PRELOAD shim (default auto).
.TP
.B ANONCHAIN_RESOLVE
1|0 — force getaddrinfo through local DoH DNS bridge.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.anonchain/config.toml
User config and profiles.
.TP
.I ~/.anonchain/sessions.db
SQLite session log.
.TP
.I /tmp/anonchain.port
Current chain port (auto-managed).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR proxychains4 (1),
.BR tor (1),
.BR iptables (8)
